 [17592186353453 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353453 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d8ef2388-0f72-5871-b0be-8276cb5fe915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353500 #edb/ref 1080 "126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353500 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353500 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "debdfcd2-ba10-5c33-a152-32714bf2926b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186351776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186351880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186353500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354137 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb52f3bb-59b4-5a00-86e6-1550bcc92127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1069 "q-84959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1071 "Sara has a box of $9$ colored pencils. In how many ways can Sara pick a set of $4$ different pencils from the box?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44e1ceb1-ad30-5708-98e7-b7ac9be19ae7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354369 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ pencils in the box, so $n=9.$ We want to select $4$ of those pencils, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential sets of four pencils is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-4)!\\,4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{5!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,024}{24} \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
